/test-contract.md", "offset": 55, "limit": 65}}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_5cvGvEluCxOB7kpiI5iOaCXy|fc_0672f30ea9308838016ad13cc391d087d1bb24e8f25db3aa8c", "name": "read", "arguments": {"path": "tests/src/org.apache.pulsar/pulsar-client-all/4.2.5/src/test/java/org_apache_pulsar/pulsar_client_all/NioDatagramChannelConfigTest.java"}}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_RULEDeUsWHFFcMFpmg7tljj6|fc_0672f30ea9308838016ad13cc391d887d181133d6333ada810", "name": "bash", "arguments": {"command": "git status --short && git log -2 --oneline"}}], "api": "openai-codex-responses", "provider": "openai-codex", "model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "usage": {"input": 2240, "output": 733, "cacheRead": 201600, "cacheWrite": 0, "reasoning": 607, "totalTokens": 204573, "cost": {"input": 0, "output": 0, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1792097458870, "responseId": "resp_0672f30ea9308838016ad13cb4eefc87d195db0d58e2d7257f", "rawStopReason": "completed"}, "toolResults": [{"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_HLBIL3MND8zG7svR2t0636Ht|fc_0672f30ea9308838016ad13cc391b887d19f0f65a7406058bd", "toolName": "read", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "@Test void recyclesObjectsThroughLocalPool() {\n    Recycler<StringBuilder> recycler = newStringBuilderRecycler();\n    StringBuilder first = recycler.get();\n    first.append(\"payload\");\n    recycler.recycle(first);\n    assertSame(first, recycler.get());\n}\n```\n\n### 1.4 Only the tested version's API\n\nA test uses only the features of the provided library version, so the suite\ncompiles and passes against the version it is written for.\n\n```java\n// Bad: JsonMapper.builder() does not exist in the tested 2.9.x line\nObjectMapper mapper = JsonMapper.builder().build();\n\n// Good: the API the tested version actually ships\nObjectMapper mapper = new ObjectMapper();\n```\n\n### 1.5 Coverage for every reporter-requested metadata need\n\nWhen an issue reports missing metadata, every metadata need inferred from the\nissue is mandatory — even when dynamic-access coverage is already complete or\nthe need is unrelated to an uncovered class. Each need is exercised through\nmeaningful public-API behavior.\n\n```java\n// Reporter stack trace names a MissingReflectionRegistrationError for\n// io.netty...BaseMpscLinkedArrayQueueProducerFields.producerIndex.\n// Cover it by driving the public API path that reaches that field:\n@Test void recyclerAllocatesFromMpscQueue() {\n    Recycler<Buffer> recycler = newBufferRecycler();\n    assertNotNull(recycler.get());   // reaches PlatformDependent.newMpscQueue(...)\n}\n```\n\n### 1.6 A 60-second bound on every individual test\n\nEvery individual test completes in under 60 seconds. Waits are bounded, and\nevery client, server, executor, and other background resource is closed so\nnothing deadlocks or keeps the JVM alive.\n\n```java\n// Bad: unbounded — a hang blocks the whole lane\nString reply = client.send(request).get();\n\n// Good: bounded wait, resource closed\ntry (MessagingClient client = newClient()) {\n    String reply = client.send(request).get(30, TimeUnit.SECONDS);\n    assertEquals(\"pong\", reply);\n}\n```\n\n### 1.7 A 10-second floor on explicit I/O timeouts\n\nEvery explicit connection, request, read, socket, server, client, process,\ndatabase, messaging, or HTTP timeout is at least 10 seconds. Shorter timeouts\nare flaky under native-image-agent metadata generation and Native Image\nstartup; unbounded waits remain forbidden (§FS-test-contract.1.6).\n\n```java\n// Bad: fine on a warm JVM, flaky under the native-image agent\n\n[457 more lines in file. Use offset=120 to continue.]"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1792097476730}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_5cvGvEluCxOB7kpiI5iOaCXy|fc_0672f30ea9308838016ad13cc391d087d1bb24e8f25db3aa8c", "toolName": "read", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "/*\n * Copyright and related rights waived via CC0\n *\n * You should have received a copy of the CC0 legalcode along with this\n * work. If not, see <http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/>.\n */\npackage org_apache_pulsar.pulsar_client_all;\n\nimport static org.assertj.core.api.Assertions.assertThat;\n\nimport java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit;\nimport org.apache.pulsar.shade.io.netty.channel.socket.DatagramChannelConfig;\nimport org.apache.pulsar.shade.io.netty.channel.socket.nio.NioDatagramChannel;\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.Timeout;\n\n@Timeout(55)\npublic class NioDatagramChannelConfigTest {\n    @Test\n    void readsAndWritesMulticastSocketOptions() {\n        NioDatagramChannel channel = new NioDatagramChannel();\n        try {\n            DatagramChannelConfig config = channel.config();\n            config.setTimeToLive(8);\n            config.setLoopbackModeDisabled(false);\n\n            assertThat(config.getTimeToLive()).isEqualTo(8);\n            assertThat(config.isLoopbackModeDisabled()).isFalse();\n        } finally {\n            channel.close().awaitUninterruptibly(10, TimeUnit.SECONDS);\n        }\n        assertThat(channel.isOpen()).isFalse();\n    }\n}\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1792097476731}, {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_RULEDeUsWHFFcMFpmg7tljj6|fc_0672f30ea9308838016ad13cc391d887d181133d6333ada810", "toolName": "bash", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": " M metadata/org.apache.pulsar/pulsar-client-all/4.2.5/reachability-metadata.json\n97090a98ba Cover Pulsar shaded dynamic-access paths\n3f6c62e9ff Bulk dynamic-access coverage (164/989)\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1792097476731}]}
