[recv] {"type": "message_start", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Role: You are an expert JVM test engineer specializing in high-coverage integration testing for external libraries.\n\nTask:\nGenerate test for `org.apache.pulsar:pulsar-client-all:4.2.5` following provided dynamic access report, by covering as many uncovered call sites as possible across all classes.\n\nSource Context:\nCoordinate: org.apache.pulsar:pulsar-client-all:4.2.5\nRepository URL: https://github.com/apache/pulsar\nMain sources:\n- URL: https://repo.maven.apache.org/maven2/org/apache/pulsar/pulsar-client-all/4.2.5/pulsar-client-all-4.2.5-sources.jar\n- Local path: local_repositories/source_context/org.apache.pulsar/pulsar-client-all/4.2.5/main\n- Files available: 7391\n\nLibrary Preparation Preflight:\nLibrary preparation preflight produced setup context.\n\nSummary: pulsar-client-all needs a live broker for meaningful producer/consumer coverage; no extra Maven dependency required since the uber-jar resolves its own transitives.\n\nAlready applied by Forge:\n- Use Docker image apachepulsar/pulsar:4.2.5 (allow-list slug apachepulsar_pulsar) (already present)\n\nAgent guidance:\nStart the container with `bin/pulsar standalone --no-functions-worker --no-stream-storage` to avoid starting the functions worker and BookKeeper-backed stream storage, which aren't needed for basic producer/consumer coverage and would otherwise slow startup. Expose ports 6650 (client serviceUrl `pulsar://localhost:6650`) and 8080 (admin HTTP, usable for readiness polling, e.g. GET /admin/v2/clusters). Pulsar standalone takes substantially longer to become ready than nats/rabbitmq (it boots a broker, bookie, and ZooKeeper in one JVM), so the test must poll/retry for readiness with a generous timeout rather than reuse the short fixed sleep pattern seen in JnatsTest. Tear down the container (docker kill/rm) after the test so repeated local runs don't leak containers.\n\nRisks:\n- Pulsar sta